  "first_lines": "J. Chem. Soc. Nigeria, Vol. 50, No. 1, pp 092 – 100 [2025]\n\n\n   QUALITY ASSESSMENT OF SOME SELECTED TOOTHPASTES USED IN NIGERIA\n\n\n\n                 *H. N. Omosigho, M. A. Balogun, H. O. Ataikiru & L. C. Obetta\n\n\n\n                     Department of Chemistry, College of Education, Warri.\n                 *CORRESPONDING AUTHOR E-mail: omosighohope@gmail.com\n\n\n\n\n                                               ABSTRACT\n\nToothpaste is a gel that is used with toothbrush to clean the teeth. They are of different brands from\ndifferent manufacturing companies hence, are made up of different compositions. In this research work,\nquality assessment of different toothpastes used in Nigeria were investigated. Five different brands of\ntoothpaste were purchased in Edjeba market Warri Delta State, Nigeria and the physical parameters,\nand heavy metals were analysed in them. Physical parameters; the pH level of the toothpastes were\ndetermined using pH meter, the moisture and volatile contents were determined using a recommended\nmethod, the heavy metals (Cadmium (Cd), Copper (Cu), Zinc (Zn), Manganese (Mn) and Lead (Pb))\nwere determined using atomic absorption spectrometer (AAS). From the results obtained, the pH value\nof these toothpastes were within 6.59 to 7.03, all the toothpastes fell within the NAFDAC recommended\npH range of 6.5 to 7.5. The moisture and volatile contents of the toothpastes were within the range of\n3.1 to 7.4 which were within the range set by NAFDAC. The heavy metals; Cd, Cu, Zn, Mn and Pb\nwere detected in all the toothpastes samples. The level of Cd ranged from 2.470 to 2.952, Cu level was\nbetween 0.096 to 5.165, the level of Zn ranged from 13.396 to 24.164, Mn concentration ranged from\n1.700 to 3.402 and Pb level was between 4.917 to 6.113. The results of the concentration of heavy\nmetals in the samples shows that some of the toothpastes contains heavy metal in an amount higher than\nthe set standards and may pose health problems to the consumers. Hence, there is need to educate the\nusers on the danger of swallowing toothpaste and how to properly use them especially for children and\npregnant women to ensure safety.\n\nKEYWORDS: Toothpaste, Heavy metals, Physical parameters, Consumers\n\n\n\nINTRODUCTION\n\nThe teeth are an important part of the body that             they used toothpick to clean the teeth, but it\nneeds to be taken care of properly. Poor oral                didn't give or enhance total dental hygiene and\nhygiene can cause oral diseases such as dental               this resulted in having cases like dental caries,\ncaries, odorous mouth, tooth decay and many                  gum diseases, mouth odor and coloured teeth.\nmore. The mouth (teeth, tongue) is the door                  This has led to the introduction of aesthetic\nthrough which we take in foods, liquid and solid             product such as toothpaste.\nsubstances into our body, for this its                       Toothpaste is a paste or gel in molten form that\nmaintenance and hygiene is necessary for                     is used with a toothbrush to clean and maintain\noverall healthiness of the body systems. This                the healthiness of teeth. Toothpaste is used to\nhas been an older practice, in the olden days,               promote oral hygiene: it is an abrasive that aids\n\n                                                     92\n\fJ. Chem. Soc. Nigeria, Vol. 50, No. 1, pp 092 – 100 [2025]\n\n\nin removing dental plaque and food from the                  Food Safety Authority (EFSA), and the Food\nteeth.[1]. Toothpaste helps to remove residue                and Drug Administration (FDA).\naccumulated on the surface of the teeth, it helps\n                                                             Fluoride (NaF)\nto remove stain, dirt, from the teeth and to keep\n                                                             Fluoride is the most popular and effective\nthe teeth surroundings neat. It is personal\n                                                             active ingredient in toothpaste to prevent dental\nhygiene product that is used every day by\n                                                             cavities. Fluoride is present in small amounts in\nchildren and adult, men and women and across",
